From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Derek Ross <derekross@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 18:46:33 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] soc: google: cpif: import Google's S5300 modem interface
 driver

Import the parts of Google's modem interface driver (CPIF,
google-modules/radio/samsung/s5300 of Google's GPL gs-6.1 kernel, the
version stock cheetah runs, CPIF-20220408R1) that boot the Samsung
S5300 over PCIe and carry its IPC and RFS channels:

- the platform driver and its device tree parsing (modem_main.c,
  modem_variation.c, modem_utils.c, modem_dump.c);
- the I/O devices: the boot and dump device, the IPC/RFS character
  devices, the network devices and the TOE device (modem_io_device.c,
  bootdump_io_device.c, ipc_io_device.c, net_io_device.c,
  modem_toe_device.c);
- the shared-memory link device and its legacy buffers, flow control,
  snapshot and debug parts (link_device*.c);
- the S5100-family modem control and its PCIe endpoint driver
  (modem_ctrl_s5100.c, modem_ctrl.c, s51xx_pcie.c);
- the shared-memory region driver (shm_ipc.c);
- the headers these include, and, under gs-include/, the six headers of
  Google's soc/gs tree they need (shm_ipc.h, modem_notifier.h,
  exynos-modem-ctrl.h, exynos-pci-noti.h, exynos-pci-ctrl.h and the
  exynos-cpif.h DT constants).

The packet processor, DIT, the throughput monitor, the PCIe IOMMU, the
S2MPU, BTL, the thermal zones and SPI boot are left out; the port runs
without them first.

The files are unchanged and not built yet; the next commit ports them to
this kernel.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Derek Ross <derekross@gmail.com>
